.TH GIT-PR-LAND-STACK 1 "2026-06-13" "git-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-pr-land-stack \- land a ready linear GitHub pull request stack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git pr-land-stack
.RI [ options ]
.I number|url|branch
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git pr-land-stack
lands a linear stack of ready GitHub pull requests from parent to child.
It composes
.BR git-pr-stack (1),
.BR git-pr-land (1),
and
.BR git-pr-restack (1).
.PP
The command refuses the whole stack before merging anything if any pull request
is not ready. As each parent lands, the next child is restacked onto the root
base branch before it is landed.
.PP
URL targets and every discovered pull request are required to belong to the
current GitHub repository before landing begins.
.PP
Repository-qualified pull request URLs are retained across discovery, landing,
restacking, and post-restack readiness polling.
.PP
Every handoff revalidates the live pull request number, head, head OID, base,
head repository, cross-repository state, and canonical URL before the next
mutation. A child restack uses the parent's original head OID as its immutable
fork boundary. The rewritten child OID is accepted only when a fresh PR record
matches the local branch. Retargeting during discovery, a parent action, or
readiness polling fails closed.
.PP
Local and remote heads are retained for manual cleanup. Stack topology is
repository-qualified, so a
same-named fork head is not treated as a base-repository parent. Cycles and
ambiguous same-repository parents fail closed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-method " " \fImethod\fR
Merge method:
.BR squash ,
.BR merge ,
or
.BR rebase .
Defaults to
.BR squash .
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-branch
Pass
.B \-\-keep\-branch
to
.BR git-pr-land (1).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print actions without changing anything.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stack was landed.
.TP
.B 1
Stack is not ready or a child restack or merge failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or local environment error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-pr-ready (1),
.BR git-pr-stack (1),
.BR git-pr-restack (1),
.BR git-pr-land (1)
